Known failure: range-stable — range-formatting one line of a multi-line statement adds ';' and re-indents a continuation line (issue to file)
An :IF condition the author split before `.AND.` / `.OR.`: each
continuation sits one level past the :IF line, the same column as the
body, the leading operator telling them apart (fmt.indent_style; style
guide continuation_line_breaks). A :WHILE condition behaves the same.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CheckLimits;
:PARAMETERS nLow, nHigh, sMode;
:DECLARE bOk;
bOk := .F.;
:IF nLow > 1
.AND. nHigh < 50
.AND. sMode == "STRICT";
bOk := .T.;
:ENDIF;
:WHILE nLow < nHigh
  .OR. bOk;
nLow += 1;
:ENDWHILE;
:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CheckLimits;
	:PARAMETERS nLow, nHigh, sMode;
	:DECLARE bOk;
	bOk := .F.;
	:IF nLow > 1
		.AND. nHigh < 50
		.AND. sMode == "STRICT";
		bOk := .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:WHILE nLow < nHigh
		.OR. bOk;
		nLow += 1;
	:ENDWHILE;
	:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
